//? Title: VOC and COCO box evaluation
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Detection evaluation must distinguish correct objects from duplicates, ignored annotations and unmatched predictions. This report derives tensor precision-envelope AP, checks VOC difficult objects and COCO crowds/caps on small fixtures, and provides an optional reader for the original externally predicted subsets. No real-dataset scores are claimed when those assets are absent.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.6_object_detection/detection_evaluation.cpp`.

> The method

Evaluation fixes model predictions and applies discrete matching, then tensor overlap, cumulative-count and recall-grid reductions. It needs no optimizer. VOC07 samples eleven recall thresholds and uses strict overlap; COCO-style box AP samples 101, includes equality and averages ten IoU cutoffs. These choices can produce different values for the same predictions.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/detection_evaluation_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/detection_evaluation_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/detection_evaluation_concept.tikz > build/detection_evaluation_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/detection_evaluation_concept.svg build/detection_evaluation_concept.dvi > build/detection_evaluation_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
