\caption(VOC and COCO box evaluation)
\alttext(Scored predictions; Annotated boxes; then Ignore and match; Per image and class; then Precision envelope; Tensor AP means.)

> Simple examples: ranked detections and the precision envelope

For each category, detections sort by descending score. If detection k is a true
positive, cumulative true positives increase; precision is `TP/(TP+FP)` and recall
is `TP/P`, where P counts nonignored ground truths. A previously matched object
cannot earn a second true positive. The envelope at recall r is the largest
precision at any later attainable recall; integrating its recall changes gives
all-point AP. VOC2007 instead samples eleven recall thresholds; COCO samples 101.

Here the score order is false positive, true positive, duplicate, true positive.
With two targets, raw precision is `[0,.5,1/3,.5]`, recall `[0,.5,.5,1]`, and the
envelope is constantly .5. All three AP definitions give .5 for this fixture.

> Architecture scope

This report defines detection matching and average-precision evaluation rather than a neural network. Its retained concept SVG shows that evaluation dataflow; detector architectures appear in the adjacent model reports.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/detection_evaluation_precision.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const std::vector<m::DetectionEvaluationTruth> truth = {{1, 0, {0, 0, 10, 10}},
                                                          {1, 0, {20, 20, 30, 30}}};
  const std::vector<m::DetectionEvaluationPrediction> predictions = {
      {1, 0, .99f, {40, 40, 50, 50}},
      {1, 0, .9f, {0, 0, 10, 10}},
      {1, 0, .8f, {0, 0, 10, 10}},
      {1, 0, .7f, {20, 20, 30, 30}}};
  const auto voc = m::EvaluateDetectionClass(predictions, truth, {1}, 0, .5, false),
             coco = m::EvaluateDetectionClass(predictions, truth, {1}, 0, .5, true);
  if (std::abs(voc.integral.item() - .5) > 1e-12 ||
      std::abs(voc.interpolated.item() - .5) > 1e-12 ||
      std::abs(coco.interpolated.item() - .5) > 1e-12)
    return 1;
  const auto tp = n::cumsum(n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{0, 1, 0, 1}), 0);
  const auto raw = tp / n::arange(1, 5).to(n::DType::Float64);
  std::print(
      "| rank | score | recall | raw precision | envelope |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
    std::print("| {} | {:.2f} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} | {:.3f} |\n", i + 1, predictions[i].score,
               voc.recall.at({i}), raw.at({i}), voc.precision.at({i}));
  auto curve = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  curve
      .lines(voc.recall.to_vector<double>(), raw.to_vector<double>(), "raw precision",
             {220, 38, 38})
      .lines(voc.recall.to_vector<double>(), voc.precision.to_vector<double>(), "envelope",
             {37, 99, 235})
      .title("Ranked precision and envelope")
      .x_label("recall")
      .y_label("precision")
      .x_limits(0, 1)
      .y_limits(0, 1.3);
  auto overlap = n::plot_tensor_map(
      n::reverse(
          n::box_iou(
              n::boxes_from_vector(std::vector<n::Box>{
                  {40, 40, 50, 50}, {0, 0, 10, 10}, {0, 0, 10, 10}, {20, 20, 30, 30}}),
              n::boxes_from_vector(std::vector<n::Box>{{0, 0, 10, 10}, {20, 20, 30, 30}})),
          {0}),
      0, 1);
  overlap.title("Prediction to truth IoU")
      .x_label("truth index")
      .y_label("prediction rank minus one")
      .x_limits(-.5, 1.5)
      .y_limits(-.5, 3.5);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2)
      .add(curve)
      .add(overlap)
      .size(1200, 550)
      .fit_panels()
      .save_svg("build/detection_evaluation_precision.svg");
  std::print("Integral AP {:.6f}; VOC07 AP {:.6f}; COCO 101-point AP {:.6f}. Line segments "
             "join ranked samples; AP uses recall increments, not trapezoidal integration of "
             "the red curve.\n",
             voc.integral.item(), voc.interpolated.item(), coco.interpolated.item());
}
```
