> Detection caps, missing categories and recall-grid arithmetic

COCO keeps the top 100 predictions **per image and category** before matching.
A correct prediction ranked 101st is therefore unavailable even if all preceding
predictions are false positives. VOC here has no detection cap.

Recall grids preserve the source implementation's floating-point construction:
`k*(1./(S-1))`. In binary arithmetic `3*.1` is slightly larger than `3/10`.
For exactly three detections out of ten targets, this source convention therefore
gives VOC07 `3/11`, alongside integral AP `.3` and COCO `31/101`. In ideal exact
arithmetic the eleven-point grid would include .3 and give `4/11`; the difference
is a numerical boundary effect, not an additional missed object. It is retained
and tested explicitly rather than silently changing the original fixture.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/detection_evaluation_cap.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  std::vector<m::DetectionEvaluationPrediction> predictions;
  for (int i = 0; i < 100; ++i)
    predictions.push_back({1, 1, 1.f - i * .001f, {30, 30, 40, 40}});
  predictions.push_back({1, 1, .1f, {0, 0, 10, 10}});
  const std::vector<m::DetectionEvaluationTruth> truth = {
      {1, 1, {0, 0, 10, 10}}, {1, 99, {0, 0, 20, 20}, false, true}};
  const auto capped = m::EvaluateDetectionClass(predictions, truth, {1}, 1, .5, true),
             uncapped = m::EvaluateDetectionClass(predictions, truth, {1}, 1, .5, false);
  if (capped.interpolated.item() != 0 || capped.recall.numel() != 100 ||
      std::abs(uncapped.integral.item() - 1. / 101) > 1e-12)
    return 1;
  const auto empty = m::EvaluateDetectionDataset({}, truth, {1}, true);
  if (empty.classes != 1 || empty.ap.item() != 0)
    return 1;
  std::vector<m::DetectionEvaluationTruth> ten;
  std::vector<m::DetectionEvaluationPrediction> three;
  for (int i = 0; i < 10; ++i) {
    const n::Box box = {float(20 * i), 0, float(20 * i + 10), 10};
    ten.push_back({1, 1, box});
    if (i < 3)
      three.push_back({1, 1, .9f - .1f * i, box});
  }
  const auto v = m::EvaluateDetectionClass(three, ten, {1}, 1, .5, false),
             c = m::EvaluateDetectionClass(three, ten, {1}, 1, .5, true);
  if (std::abs(v.interpolated.item() - 3. / 11) > 1e-12 ||
      std::abs(v.integral.item() - .3) > 1e-12 ||
      std::abs(c.interpolated.item() - 31. / 101) > 1e-12)
    return 1;
  auto q = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  q.lines(n::arange(95, 102).to_vector<double>(),
          n::slice_axis(uncapped.recall, 0, 94, 101).to_vector<double>(),
          "VOC uncapped recall", {37, 99, 235})
      .lines(n::arange(95, 101).to_vector<double>(),
             n::slice_axis(capped.recall, 0, 94, 100).to_vector<double>(),
             "COCO capped recall", {220, 38, 38})
      .title("A correct box ranked 101st")
      .x_label("detection rank")
      .y_label("recall")
      .x_limits(95, 102)
      .y_limits(0, 1.3);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  q.size(900, 500).save_svg("build/detection_evaluation_cap.svg");
  std::print(
      "Cap100 AP {:.6f}; uncapped integral AP {:.12f}; selected categories {} (crowd-only "
      "class 99 excluded). Three-of-ten: VOC07 {:.12f}, integral {:.12f}, COCO {:.12f}.\n",
      capped.interpolated.item(), uncapped.integral.item(), empty.classes,
      v.interpolated.item(), v.integral.item(), c.interpolated.item());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Cap100 AP 0.000000; uncapped integral AP 0.009900990099; selected categories 1 (crowd-only class 99 excluded). Three-of-ten: VOC07 0.272727272727, integral 0.300000000000, COCO 0.306930693069.
\image(figures/detection_evaluation_cap.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The correct detection at rank 101 lifts uncapped recall to one. The COCO curve ends at rank 100 with zero recall. This fixture isolates the cap from score or localization errors.)
\alttext(The correct detection at rank 101 lifts uncapped recall to one. The COCO curve ends at rank 100 with zero recall. This fixture isolates the cap from score or localization errors.)

> Optional prepared VOC/COCO subsets

The original C++ port is itself an evaluator: it consumes `predictions.json`
exported by an external TensorFlow SSD MobileNet-v2 run. It does not load that
SavedModel or train a detector. Those predictions and annotated subsets are not
available in this checkout's dataset cache, so the executed results above are
synthetic evaluator fixtures, **not VOC or COCO benchmark measurements**.

This optional import uses the retained example data readers and the canonical
tensor evaluator. Set `DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR` to the datasets root containing
`detection_eval/voc2007` and `detection_eval/coco2017`. Each subset contains
`images.tsv`, `annotations.tsv` and `predictions.json`. VOC coordinates must
already have been converted from one-based inclusive to zero-based half-open;
COCO JSON `[x,y,w,h]` boxes become `[y,x,y+h,x+w]`. Category IDs remain the
original COCO IDs. All numerical evaluation now forwards to the tensor library.
No optimizer is appropriate: the inputs are fixed predictions, not fitted leaves.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge) -I../../../../../../examples/nn"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include "common/detection_evaluation.hpp"
#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace m = dm::nn::models;
  namespace io = detection_evaluation;
  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  int evaluated = 0;
  for (const auto &name : {"voc2007", "coco2017"}) {
    const auto directory = cache / "detection_eval" / name;
    if (!std::filesystem::exists(directory / "images.tsv") ||
        !std::filesystem::exists(directory / "annotations.tsv") ||
        !std::filesystem::exists(directory / "predictions.json")) {
      std::print("{}: prepared images/annotations/predictions unavailable; no real-dataset "
                 "metric computed.\n",
                 name);
      continue;
    }
    const auto images = io::LoadEvaluationImages(directory);
    const auto truth = io::TensorTruth(io::LoadEvaluationTruth(directory));
    const auto predictions =
        io::TensorPredictions(io::LoadPredictionsJson(directory / "predictions.json"));
    std::vector<int> ids;
    for (const auto &image : images)
      ids.push_back(image.id);
    const auto metrics =
        m::EvaluateDetectionDataset(predictions, truth, ids, std::string(name) == "coco2017");
    std::print("{}: {} images, {} truths, {} predictions, {} evaluated classes; AP50 {:.6f}, "
               "AP75 {:.6f}, AP50:95 {:.6f}, VOC07 {:.6f}.\n",
               name, images.size(), truth.size(), predictions.size(), metrics.classes,
               metrics.ap50.item(), metrics.ap75.item(), metrics.ap.item(),
               metrics.voc07.item());
    ++evaluated;
  }
  std::print("Evaluated {} prepared subsets.\n", evaluated);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
voc2007: prepared images/annotations/predictions unavailable; no real-dataset metric computed.
coco2017: prepared images/annotations/predictions unavailable; no real-dataset metric computed.
Evaluated 0 prepared subsets.
// result_end


> Conclusion

The executed fixtures expose ranked precision, duplicates, ignored objects, threshold equality, missing categories, a rank-101 detection and the source recall-grid boundary convention. Eight native tests also compare randomized results to an independent host reference. The optional loader evaluates prepared external predictions without training or invoking TensorFlow; its absent assets are reported explicitly.

> References

- [PASCAL VOC2007 official challenge and development kit](https://www.robots.ox.ac.uk/~vgg/projects/pascal/VOC/voc2007/index.html).
- [COCO official evaluator, cocoeval.py](https://github.com/cocodataset/cocoapi/blob/master/PythonAPI/pycocotools/cocoeval.py).
- [Everingham et al. (2010), The PASCAL Visual Object Classes (VOC) Challenge](https://doi.org/10.1007/s11263-009-0275-4).
